PsyCross then reported invalid tag lengths 99 and 136, malformed primitive
length diagnostics, and stopped with SIGSEGV:
  ParsePrimitivesLinkedList(p=0x5f2064) LIBGPU/PsyX_GPU.cpp:906
  DrawOTag(p=0x5f2064) LIBGPU.C:456
  wm_tail_draw_otag() world_map_frame_tail_71984.c:93

Conclusion:
  retail OT = 0x400 four-byte entries in 0x1000 bytes;
  production binary defines USE_EXTENDED_PRIM_POINTERS=0;
  GDB sizeof(unsigned long)=8, sizeof(OT_TAG)=8, sizeof(P_TAG)=8;
  ClearOTagR therefore strides 8 bytes and spans 0x2000 bytes;
  root+0xffc is not a host OT_TAG boundary, and guest callback links such as
  0x0009d310 are not host links for nextPrim. This is a class-(e) OT
  ABI/layout/link-namespace boundary. No production fix or second-frame
  iteration was committed. DrawOTag crash means stop per task.
